@startuml warren_adaptive_model_uml
' The Warren Adaptive Model - UML Activity Diagram
' CSC505 Critical Thinking | C. Warren
' Adapted from Pressman & Maxim (2020); feedback loops from Agile (Beck et al., 2001),
' Spiral risk analysis (Boehm, 1988), and DevOps continuous delivery (Humble & Farley, 2010).

title <b>The Warren Adaptive Model</b>\n<size:11>UML Activity Diagram | CSC505 Critical Thinking | Adapted from Pressman & Maxim (2020)</size>

skinparam dpi 180
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #1D4ED8
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ActivityFontColor #1E3A8A
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B45309
skinparam ActivityDiamondFontColor #78350F
skinparam ArrowColor #111827
skinparam ArrowFontColor #B45309
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7ED
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B45309
skinparam NoteFontColor #7C2D12
skinparam TitleFontSize 20

start

repeat
  :<b>1. Discovery & Communication</b>\n<size:11>Continuous stakeholder collaboration; evolving</size>\n<size:11>requirements captured as a prioritized backlog</size>;

  :<b>2. Adaptive Planning</b>\n<size:11>Rolling-wave estimates, risk analysis (Spiral),</size>\n<size:11>re-planned at every iteration boundary</size>;

  note right
    Every phase ends with a
    <b>feedback checkpoint</b>: failed
    reviews loop work back one
    phase instead of letting
    defects flow downstream
    (Royce, 1970)
  end note

  repeat
    :<b>3. Iterative Modeling</b>\n<size:11>Lightweight analysis & design; prototypes</size>\n<size:11>validated with users before construction</size>;

    :<b>4. Incremental Construction</b>\n<size:11>Short build-test cycles; test-driven development,</size>\n<size:11>continuous integration, peer review</size>;

  backward :refine design\n& rebuild;
  repeat while (Increment accepted?) is ([no]) not ([yes])

  :<b>5. Continuous Deployment & Monitoring</b>\n<size:11>Automated delivery pipeline (DevOps); telemetry</size>\n<size:11>and user feedback feed the next increment</size>;

backward :continuous feedback loop:\ntelemetry, user feedback,\nnew requirements;
repeat while (Continue product evolution?) is ([yes]\nnext increment) not ([no])

:product retired /\nmajor release milestone;

stop

legend bottom
  <b>Warren Adaptive Model</b> - C. Warren, CSC505.
  Feedback loops adapted from Agile (Beck et al., 2001), Spiral risk
  analysis (Boehm, 1988), and DevOps continuous delivery (Humble & Farley, 2010).
end legend

@enduml
